+/// the result once. On PyTorch 2.10.0's CPU kernel that equals the F32 value
+/// `x * sigmoid(x)` rounded to the dtype on every finite BF16 input and on
+/// all but one F16 input, where F32 evaluation order decides a near-tie
+/// (MPS differs further only by flushing BF16 subnormals to zero). Burn's
+/// `activation::silu` is the two-operation graph `x * sigmoid(x)`: in half
+/// precision the sigmoid is rounded to the activation dtype before the
+/// product, whose rounding then adds a second error. Near zero the rounded
+/// sigmoid loses the `x^2 / 4` term of `x / 2 + x^2 / 4`; for larger `|x|`
+/// the second rounding is off by one unit in the last place. Gated MLPs feed
+/// every such difference into the residual stream of every block.
